Z||000000||Steven||04-01-2001||06:05 PM||||Can anyone tell me the difference between the 2.5 engine in the 84 Fiero, and the 2.5 engine in the early - mid 80's S-10 pick up trucks?||||reg||5
Z||000001||LuckyTheyWereEverMade||04-01-2001||06:58 PM||||The starter is on the other side for rear wheel drive applications.  Also, the S10 block may have some extra webbing to strengthen the block.<P>Most say that a 1988 4cyl Fiero crankshaft is better than the other years.  But most of the better duke blocks have a different motor mount locations.  For this reason, the majority of Duke engines either stay stock or get super duty parts.  <P>Super duty parts cost a lot nowadays.  Here's a site that sells them:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.gtsonline.com/krp/prod1.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.gtsonline.com/krp/prod1.htm</A> <P>Here's a site that will tell you everything you need to know about the Iron Duke:<BR> <A HREF="http://fiero2m4.homestead.com/index.html" TARGET=_blank>http://fiero2m4.homestead.com/index.html</A> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||Steven||04-01-2001||10:22 PM||||So even if I can get a great deal on a S-10 engine, it won't do me any good, because it won't work?||||reg||1
